From: Sirius port
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] soc: qcom: spm: drive the MSM8974 Krait supply from the L2 SAW

On MSM8974 the four Krait cores share one supply: ganged PM8841 FTS phases,
reached over SPMI by the L2 SAW2, which Qualcomm's downstream tree marks as
the APCS master (qcom,L2-spm-is-apcs-master). Voltage, phase count and
PWM/PFM mode are all sent through that SAW's VCTL register. Mainline has the
SPM regulator framework, but only the APQ8064 SAW2 v1.1 implements set_vdd,
the msm8974 L2 compatible has no match entry, and spm_get_cpu() rejects any
SAW that no CPU references through qcom,saw.

Add the MSM8974 L2 SAW as a regulator:

  - register offsets for SAW2 v2.1 from msm-3.10 spm-v2.c: PMIC_STS 0x14,
    RST 0x18, VCTL 0x1c, PMIC_DATA_3 0x4c
  - CFG 0x14, PMIC_DATA_0 0x02030080, PMIC_DATA_1 0x00030000, as written by
    Sony's Xperia Z2 device tree (qcom,spm@f9012000)
  - voltage: level = uV / 5 mV into VCTL port 0 and PMIC_DATA_3, confirmed
    by the level echoed back in PMIC_STS (downstream set_pmic_gang_voltage
    and msm_spm_drv_set_vctl2)
  - at probe, before the initial voltage: PWM mode on port 2 and all four
    phases on port 1. Downstream scales both with load; holding them costs
    idle power but cannot starve the cores at the top operating points
  - initial voltage 900 mV, downstream's CORE_VOLTAGE_BOOTUP
  - an APCS master is not bound to a CPU, so its writes run on CPU0

Also skip the sequence write for a SAW with no SEQ_ENTRY offset. Offset 0
is the start of the control registers, which the unguarded copy would
otherwise zero.

Measured on a Z2 before this change: every core reports APC_PWR_GATE_CTL
0x403f3f7f (BHS enabled on all segments, LDO bypassed and powered down), so
core voltage follows this rail directly. The L2 SAW reads version
0x20010000 (v2.1) with the PMIC-arbiter bit set in ID.

